Company Introduction

We are a company specializing in energy services and digital solutions, committed to providing clients with stable, efficient, and reliable comprehensive service support through professional technology, project management capabilities, and innovative service models.

The company continuously develops in the fields of energy operation, technical services, project management, data application, and enterprise digital construction, accumulating professional experience in energy system services, operational optimization, technical support, and digital applications. By combining industry experience with modern technology, the company continuously improves service efficiency, operational capabilities, and customer experience, providing flexible and professional solutions for different business scenarios.

As the global energy industry continues to evolve towards digitalization, intelligence, and efficiency, we continuously upgrade our corporate capabilities, actively exploring the application of data technology, intelligent tools, and modern management systems in the energy and related business areas, further improving our integrated service system from technical support to project operation and customer service.

The company adheres to a customer-centric approach, with professionalism, efficiency, innovation, and long-term cooperation as its development philosophy. We value talent cultivation, technological innovation, and teamwork, continuously improving our comprehensive service capabilities to provide clients with more stable, professional, and sustainably valuable services.

Looking ahead, we will continue to deepen our business layout in the energy sector, continuously strengthen our technological R&D, project management, and digital service capabilities, expand international business cooperation, and build a more comprehensive global customer service system, striving to become an energy and digital solutions company with professional strength and long-term service capabilities.

Job Overview

The Executive Director of Global Partnerships is a senior management position responsible for the execution of the company's global strategic partnerships, international partnerships, business alliances, and collaborative projects.

This position typically reports to the Chief Business Officer (CBO), Chief Strategy Officer (CSO), Global Business Head, or Chief Executive Officer (CEO), and is responsible for translating the company's global partnership strategy into concrete collaborative projects and business results, coordinating cross-regional partner development, major cooperation negotiations, project implementation, and the construction of the collaborative ecosystem.

Core Responsibilities

I. Global Partnership Strategy Planning
Develop global strategic partnership development plans and annual implementation schemes; Identify key cooperation regions and industries based on the company's global business strategy; Analyze international market, industry trends, and competitive landscape; Establish a global partner screening and evaluation system; Ensure that the partnership strategy is aligned with the company's overall development goals.

II. Global Strategic Partner Development
Develop key global enterprises, platforms, institutions, and industry partners;
Establish and maintain long-term strategic partnerships;
Expand cross-regional and cross-industry cooperation opportunities;
Manage the lifecycle of key partners;
Build a global partner network.

III. Major Cooperation Project Execution
Oversee the entire process of strategic cooperation projects, from opportunity identification to implementation;
Develop project objectives, timelines, resource plans, and delivery standards;
Coordinate product, sales, marketing, operations, finance, and legal teams;
Resolve execution obstacles in cross-regional cooperation;
Ensure major cooperation projects are completed on schedule.

IV. Business Negotiation and Agreement Management
Participate in or lead major international business negotiations;
Develop cooperation frameworks, business models, and terms;
Coordinate with legal and financial teams to complete agreement review;
Promote the signing of strategic cooperation agreements;
Continuously maintain important partnerships.

V. Cooperation Commercialization and Revenue Growth
Identify new revenue streams driven by cooperation;
Promote joint sales, channel cooperation, joint marketing, and product cooperation;
Evaluate the commercial value and return on investment of cooperation projects;
Drive the conversion of customer and business opportunities brought by partners;
Enhance the contribution of strategic cooperation to corporate revenue growth.

VI. Global Ecosystem Development
Establish a global partner ecosystem;
Promote the development of industry alliances, channel networks, and business ecosystems;
Establish partner operation and empowerment mechanisms;
Facilitate resource synergy among partners;
Enhance the company's global industry influence.

VII. Cross-Regional Coordination
Coordinate cooperation teams in North America, Europe, Asia Pacific, and other regions;
Establish global cooperation project management standards;
Balance headquarters strategy with local market needs;
Promote cross-regional cooperation resource sharing;
Improve the efficiency of global cooperation execution.

VIII. Management Decision Support
Submit global cooperation analysis reports to the CEO, CSO, CBO, and other senior management;
Analyze strategic cooperation opportunities, market risks, and competitive changes;
Provide advice for major cooperation and market entry decisions;
Establish a global cooperation performance reporting system.

IX. Team Building
Establish a global strategic cooperation management team;
Guide regional cooperation leaders and senior business development personnel;
Develop team goals, budgets, and performance systems;
Cultivate global business cooperation and ecosystem management talent.

Job Qualifications

Education Background: Bachelor's degree or above; Major in International Business, Business Administration, Marketing, Strategic Management, Economics, or related fields; MBA, EMBA, or advanced degree in International Business preferred.

Work Experience: 20+ years of experience in strategic partnerships, business development, corporate development, or international business; 8-15+ years of experience in senior strategic partnerships or global business management; Experience as Executive Director (Global Partnerships), Global Partnerships Director, VP (Strategic Partnerships), or Business Development Executive; Experience with multinational corporations or global market cooperation projects.

Show more

Show less

Seniority level

Director

Employment type

Full-time

Job function

Business Development and Sales

Industries

Oil and Gas

